{
  "dom_id": "step-q147611",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/27c1ad7d429eb8da46b0bb3baec048b3564ce206b4523416cb4cb56b0a33767f.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(3,-6)$, $(0,0),$ $(6,-12).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062587/assets/9c045d6467a91676cd27a4c11cbb651a798b2480662d09b446b52d8eeb490ff4.png)",
